[CENTER][FONT=Book Antiqua][SIZE=5]Continuation of the well-known Cron plugin - [URL='https://www.spigotmc.org/resources/mc-cron-scheduler-jobs-bungeecord-support.37632/']MC-Cron.[/URL]
All credits goes to the original author - TheTadeSK.[/SIZE][/FONT]
[/CENTER]
[FONT=Book Antiqua][SIZE=4][COLOR=#000000]SRV-Cron is a all-in-one minecraft server scheduler that has many features to schedule jobs for certain times or in-game events.

It is a continuation of a well-known Cron plugin - MC-Cron with a lot of additional and expanded features that original MC-Cron plugin does not provide, such as PlaceholderAPI support, sending commands as players, variable actions and condition checking.[/COLOR]
[FONT=Book Antiqua][SIZE=4][B]Current release:[/B] 2.14.0 · [B]Target:[/B] Paper 26.2 · [B]Java:[/B] 25[/SIZE][/FONT]
[FONT=Book Antiqua][FONT=Book Antiqua][FONT=Book Antiqua][U]_________________________________________________[/U][/FONT][/FONT][/FONT][/SIZE][/FONT]
[SIZE=4][FONT=Book Antiqua]
[FONT=Book Antiqua][FONT=Book Antiqua][FONT=Book Antiqua][FONT=Book Antiqua][SIZE=5][B]# FEATURES[/B][/SIZE][/FONT][/FONT][/FONT][/FONT][/FONT][/SIZE]

[FONT=Book Antiqua][SIZE=4]These are some of the features that this plugin provides.[/SIZE]

[B][B]•[/B][/B] Customizable jobs;
[B][B]• [/B][/B]Console, player, and operator command execution;
[B][B]•[/B][/B] Execute commands by every online player;
[B][B]•[/B][/B] Send messages, titles, and action bars;
[B][B]•[/B][/B] Play sounds and spawn particle effects;
[B][B]•[/B][/B] Broadcast messages and write scheduled logs;
[B][B]•[/B][/B] Filter actions by permissions, PlaceholderAPI values, or scoreboard scores;
[B][B]•[/B][/B] Event jobs & commands;
[B][B]•[/B][/B] Start-up commands;
[B][B]•[/B][/B] Delayed command execution (/timer);
[B][B]•[/B][/B] [B]BungeeCord [/B]support;
[B][B]•[/B][/B] [B]PlaceholderAPI [/B]support[B];[/B][/FONT]

[FONT=Book Antiqua][B]COMMAND ACTIONS & CONDITIONS[/B]
Scheduled commands run as the console by default. Action prefixes can send messages, show titles or action bars, play sounds, spawn particles, chat or run commands as a player, run commands as an operator, broadcast, or log output.

Supported prefixes: [B][MESSAGE]/[TEXT], [TITLE], [ACTIONBAR], [SOUND], [PARTICLE], [CHAT], [PLAYER], [OP], [CONSOLE], [BROADCAST], [LOG], and [LOG with a file name][/B].

Messages, titles, action bars, and broadcasts support MiniMessage and legacy &/§ color codes, including RGB formats. Prefix conditions support permissions, PlaceholderAPI comparisons (when PlaceholderAPI is installed), scoreboard scores, and combinations using [B]&&[/B] and [B]||[/B]:
[code]
- '{IF:hasPermission:vip} [MESSAGE] <gold>Welcome, %player_name%!'
- '{IF:placeholder:%vault_eco_balance%>=1000} [CONSOLE] give %player_name% diamond 1'
- '{IF:score:points>=10} [ACTIONBAR] &aYou have enough points.'
[/code]
Conditions require a player context, such as an event job or a command dispatched for &lt;ALL&gt;/&lt;ALL+&gt;. Existing action-header filters such as [TEXT (PERMISSION:staff)] ... remain supported.
</FONT>

[FONT=Book Antiqua][B]AVAILABLE EVENTS[/B]
(Use these values in configuration)
- join-event
- quit-event
- weather-change-event
- world-load-event
- player-bed-enter-event
- player-bed-leave-event
- player-change-world-event
- player-gamemode-change-event
- player-kick-event
- chat-event
- command-event
- item-pickup-event
- player-advancement-done-event

[B]GENERIC PAPER/BUKKIT EVENT JOBS[/B]
Use [B]generic-event-jobs[/B] to register any Bukkit/Paper [B]Event[/B] class
that provides the standard [B]HandlerList[/B], including events from enabled
plugins. Configure the fully qualified class name, event priority,
cancelled-event handling, optional player/world getter paths, property aliases,
and jobs. Public zero-argument [B]getX()/isX()[/B] getters are supported, with
numeric [B][index][/B] access for lists and arrays. Use [B]{event.<path>}[/B]
directly or give a path a shorter name under [B]placeholders[/B]. Event values
are captured when the event fires, including for delayed jobs.

[code=YAML]
generic-event-jobs:
  item-pickup:
    event: org.bukkit.event.player.PlayerAttemptPickupItemEvent
    priority: NORMAL
    ignore-cancelled: false
    context:
      player: player
      world: player.world
    placeholders:
      item_type: item.itemStack.type
      item_amount: item.itemStack.amount
    jobs:
      announce:
        time: 0
        commands:
          - '[MESSAGE] Picked up {event.item.itemStack.amount} {item_type}'
[/code]

Player and world context are inferred when an event exposes one unambiguous
value; configure [B]context.player[/B] or [B]context.world[/B] to select a
getter path when needed. Existing [B]event-jobs[/B] and BungeeCord join/quit
events remain available.

[B]BUILT-IN PLACEHOLDERS[/B]
- {[B]player_name}[/B] - for events that relate to a player.
- {[B]world_name}[/B] - for events that relate to a world.

.. and bunch more event-specific placeholders, read more at:
[URL]https://github.com/M0diis/SRV-Cron/wiki/Configuration#events[/URL]

You can use both placeholders if event relates to both player and a world (ex. player-change-world-event)

[B]BungeeCord has only two events available, join & quit.[/B]
[SIZE=4][FONT=Book Antiqua][FONT=Book Antiqua][FONT=Book Antiqua][FONT=Book Antiqua][U]_________________________________________________[/U][/FONT][/FONT][/FONT][/FONT][/SIZE][/FONT]
[SIZE=4][FONT=Book Antiqua]
[FONT=Book Antiqua][FONT=Book Antiqua][FONT=Book Antiqua][FONT=Book Antiqua][SIZE=5][B]# COMMANDS & PERMISIONS[/B][/SIZE][/FONT][/FONT][/FONT][/FONT][/FONT][/SIZE]

[FONT=Book Antiqua][B]RUN COMMAND AFTER SPECIFIED SECONDS[/B]
Command: /timer <seconds> <command>
Permission: srvcron.command.timer

[B]RELOAD CONFIGURATION & JOBS[/B]
Command: /srvcron reload
Permission: srvcron.command.reload

[B]RUN CRON OR EVENT JOB MANUALLY[/B]
Command: /srvcron run <job-name> or /srvcron run event <event-name>
Permission: srvcron.command.run

[B]SUSPEND JOB EXECUTION[/B]
Command: /srvcron suspend <job-name>
Permission: srvcron.command.suspend

[B]RESUME JOB EXECUTION[/B]
Command: /srvcron resume <job-name>
Permission: srvcron.command.resume

[B]JOB INFORMATION[/B]
Command: /srvcron jobinfo <job-name>
Permission: srvcron.command.jobinfo

[B]JOB & EVENT LIST[/B]
Command: /srvcron list [events]
Permission: srvcron.command.list
